  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nShowers and storms will move across the region today. There is the\npotential for severe weather with these storms with damaging wind the\nprimary threat and also the potential for some hail as well. Heavy\nrain will occur and with the west to east orientation there is some\nflooding concerns as well. Going into the evening and into Thursday\nmorning there is another signal for west to east oriented showers \nand storms. The latest runs have come in a little further south with \nthis, however there is a concern across far southern portions of the \nforecast area that additional rainfall could occur.\n\nAdditional thunderstorms will develop on Thursday in advance of a\ncold front that moves through Friday morning. Confidence is lower in\nsevere weather during the day on Thursday. The better potential if\nsevere weather occurs on Thursday would be closer to the front.\n\nThe cold front moves through Friday morning. Expect gusty winds with\nwinds in excess of 30 mph possible. Temperatures will fall during the\nday on Friday.\n\nKey Message 2)\n\nCooler air will continue to work into the area and expect\ntemperatures to drop down into the 30s in many locations by Saturday\nmorning. Winds will stay up some through Friday night and therefore\nwhile patchy frost cannot be ruled out, not expecting a widespread\nfrost. Sunday morning will have the best potential for a widespread\nfrost. Temperatures drop into the low to middle 30s under good\nradiational cooling conditions. After the cool morning Sunday\nmorning, temperatures start to increase into next week.",
